  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Medicines to Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partner: Caritas Zamosc-Lubacz&#xF3;w
Funding: JustGiving Medicines to Ukraine page.
Total number of direct beneficiaries (individuals): 10,000

Context: Pharmacists across Europe have responded to the increasing calls for specialist help from Ukrainian hospitals by launching a campaign. Led by their national pharmacists&#x2019; organisations, pharmacists are using their expertise around medicines to organize the sourcing, logistics and the safe delivery of specialist medicines to where it is most needed by Ukrainian casualties.

Key activities: Mobilising various pharmacist union organisations in countries that are members of a European umbrella pharmacy union called EPhEU; centralise the final place of transferring the funds so that financial transactions are carried out optimally; transferring the medicines using a quality logistical chain to the intended destination with the support of the Polish and Ukrainian authorities where necessary; ensuring that the medicines are suitable for human consumption.

Activity split:
100%: Health in emergencies

Extended to August 2024 with the intention to send the final tranche of funds in Jun-Jul 2024 and the Medicines to Ukraine JustGiving page to be closed by PDA / EPhEU. However, Caritas Zamosc-Lubaczow no longer want to be part of the project so a new project partner will need to be identified for the remaining funds (&#xA3;48,290.97). All funds donated to JustGiving page Medicines to Ukraine from 1st June 2024 will be retained in the CAFOD Ukraine Emergency Appeal (SD1074); all project partners notified of this decision.</narrative>
  </description>
